<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>

  <!-- ============================================================================
       Compatibility: Appliances Expanded (scpchemfuel.appliances)
       Maps AE's chemfuel-powered workbenches to the matching animated tool by appending
       their defNames to existing tools' <workbenchDefs>. Gated behind PatchOperationFindMod
       (matched on the mod's display NAME), so nothing touches our defs when AE isn't loaded.

       AE's benches all use RecipeInheritanceExtension to inherit the vanilla recipe set from
       the bench they mimic, so the same hand-tool that fits the vanilla bench fits the AE one.
       No new JobToolDefs or sprites are needed — pure workbenchDefs appends.

       Auto-covered WITHOUT a patch (left here as a note):
         SCP_ChemDrill (chemfuel excavator) — its WorkGiver subclasses WorkGiver_DeepDrill, so it
           issues the OperateDeepDrill job that JE_Tool_Auger already keys on.

       Intentionally NO tool:
         CA_ChemfuelCrematorium — cremation; vanilla ElectricCrematorium has no tool either.
         CE_ChemfuelPot (soup pot) / CA_InfiniteDeepchemPumpjack — automated processors
           (AdvancedResourceProcessor / DeepExtractor), no worker DoBill job to animate.

       Conditional benches (CE_ChemfuelDeepFrier/Grill, CE_AirFryer, CA_ChemfuelStoveLarge,
       CE_FueledSmithyLarge) only exist when VCE / VFE-Production is also active; listing their
       defNames here is inert when those modules aren't loaded (plain-string bench match, same
       as our Medieval Overhaul entries).

       Bench -> tool:
         chemfuel stove                       -> spoon (cook stir + steam)
         chemfuel deep fryer / grill / air f. -> spoon  (VCE)
         large chemfuel stove                 -> spoon  (VFE-Production)
         chemfuel smithy                      -> bench welder + mask (tech-gated -> smith hammer pre-Electricity)
         large chemfuel smithy                -> bench welder + mask  (VFE-Production)
         chemfuel smelter                     -> glowing smelt rod
       ============================================================================ -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Appliances Expanded</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <!-- Cooking: chemfuel stove (core), VCE deep fryer / grill / air fryer,
             VFE-Production large chemfuel stove. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/JobEffects.JobToolDef[defName="JE_Tool_Spoon"]/workbenchDefs</xpath>
          <value>
            <li>CE_ChemfuelStove</li>
            <li>CE_ChemfuelDeepFrier</li>
            <li>CE_ChemfuelGrill</li>
            <li>CE_AirFryer</li>
            <li>CA_ChemfuelStoveLarge</li>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- Smithing: chemfuel smithy (core) + VFE-Production large chemfuel smithy.
             Both are fuel-fired, so the Electricity tech-gate shows a hammer & anvil
             pre-Electricity and the bench welder + mask afterwards. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/JobEffects.JobToolDef[defName="JE_Tool_BenchWelder"]/workbenchDefs</xpath>
          <value>
            <li>CA_ChemfuelSmithy</li>
            <li>CE_FueledSmithyLarge</li>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- Smelting: chemfuel smelter. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/JobEffects.JobToolDef[defName="JE_Tool_SmeltRod"]/workbenchDefs</xpath>
          <value>
            <li>CA_ChemfuelSmelter</li>
          </value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
